From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:33 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource-packs): apply dependencies and selected
 subpacks

Resolve pack order from manifest dependencies while preserving server precedence for unrelated packs. Overlay the server-selected subpack before conversion and key the converted cache by effective content so variants cannot share a stale Java pack.

A server can name a subpack that the pack manifest does not declare. Select the root pack and log a warning instead of failing the stack. The Hive does this for every pack: a native 1.26.60.5 capture (protocol 2225) shows its ResourcePacksInfo subpack field holding each pack's own header name, for example 'HiveDR' for e50e60aa-3c1c-3562-abb0-b741b2eeed07 0.0.1, and none of its 23 pack manifests declares a subpack. The native client joins these servers, so it has no variant to apply and loads the root pack.

